[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue with one fix queued. Read report by report, it holds
three problems. Each needs its own fix, and each now has its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
The parser fix queued for #4471 does not close #4471. The booking-v3 form and the one-day moves
stay broken after it ships.
</Callout>

## What is in #4471

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

This is the desk's own view of #4471, built from the ticket export at render time. Each row, and
the footnote under it, is one problem with its own ticket:

| in the table | problem | ticket |
| --- | --- | --- |
| row `parser` | the shared parser reads day-first dates month first | <a href="{repo}/1">#1</a> |
| row `hint` | the booking-v3 form hints `MM/DD/YYYY`, then reads the date day first | <a href="{repo}/2">#2</a> |
| footnote: read as a one-day move | the booking lands one day early, not flipped | <a href="{repo}/3">#3</a> |

Each ticket counts its reports the way this table does. The one-day moves are filed under
`parser` by tenant, so they count in the `parser` row and in #3.

## How to tell them apart

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first, and every tenant on file writes
  the day first. The day and the month swap: 2 March becomes 3 February. It reaches every channel
  of every tenant.
- **`hint`**: the booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field, but reads what people
  type the tenant's way, day first. People follow the hint, and the date swaps. Only reports that
  came in through the form, at a tenant on booking-v3. Fixing the parser does not fix this; the
  hint has to match what the form reads.
- **one-day move**: the booking moves by one day, not by a swap. Tuesday becomes Monday, one
  client gets Tuesday while another in a different time zone gets Monday, an invite arrives
  before the booking was made. That looks like a time zone shift when the date is stored or sent,
  not a parser bug. The desk listed these reports in its notes, but no fix covers them.

## Why one ticket hid three

- Triage merges on the subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)).
  "Wrong date" fits all three problems, so all three landed in one ticket. Merging on subject
  alone needs a cause check before it.
- The intake tag is a guess from the reporter's browser, not from the tenant: the "tagged as"
  column shows how often it disagrees. Group by tenant, form and channel, as `causes.ts` does.
- The table above already marked `hint` as "no ticket of its own" and footnoted the one-day
  moves. Status `known` made it read as finished.

